@title bit Generations - Dial Hex (Japan)
@file Bit Generations Dial Hex (J).gba
@game BVBJ
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@known * checkpoint solo_board: -- §101 (Dial Hex): the triangles come from a generator seeded with TM1CNT_L (prescaler 1024) at f494; dingbat reads 0x0E8A, mgba 0x0E89, the second reference 0x0F24. Timer 1 starts on the same cycle in dingbat and mgba (f2), but mgba counts the prescaler from the enable and dingbat from one free-running divider (the AGB SP's, hwprobe TIMPHASE); the enable lands about 65 cycles before a divider tick, so dingbat counts one tick more by the read. The second reference is 154 ticks ahead from its boot entry (§85)
@known * audio differs from both references -- §101 (Dial Hex): the three piles grow from different triangles (solo_board) and only mgba's completes a hexagon (f10964), so the fall and clear sounds part from f4785 on; the references meet only where both are quiet or both repeat the same fall sound
# SOLO, played hands-off to GAME OVER: the triangles fall until the hexagon
# is full. A from GAME OVER returns to the title and the game has written its
# 12-byte record ("JBVB", the best score at byte 4, a checksum at 10-11).
# [load]: the title and the mode menu look the same with or without a save
# (nothing on screen shows the record), then SOLO and its pause menu.
# Finding (solo_board on): every emulator is dealt other triangles from the
# same inputs (see @known; docs/playtest-bugs.md §101, Dial Hex).
# With no input mgba's pile happens to complete a green hexagon (f10964) and
# its GAME OVER comes ~5,300 frames after dingbat-bios's and the second
# reference's (both by f13964); the best scores saved are 2 (dingbat-bios),
# 13 (mgba) and 1 (the second reference), so the three saves differ.

[new]
wait 300
checkpoint warning window=30
press A
wait 500
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint mode_menu window=30
press R after=60
checkpoint solo_selected window=30
press START after=120
checkpoint solo_board window=30
wait 540
wait 3000
wait 6000
wait 3000
wait 600
wait 5000
checkpoint game_over window=30 compare=text
press A after=120
press START after=120
checkpoint menu_after window=30

[load]
wait 300
press A
wait 440
checkpoint title_loaded window=30
wait 60
press START
wait 60
checkpoint menu_loaded window=30
press R after=60
press START after=120
wait 200
press START after=60
checkpoint pause_loaded window=0 compare=text
